  "model_vision_findings": "Inspected all fifteen native/before/current full pages, 5% pixel diffs and matched heading/list crops at full 150 DPI, including the before Item E shift crop. The primary child markers and their numbering indents are now absent as in Word; the four-level probes also suppress Item D, B/E/G or C according to the active level. Explicit paragraph indentation on suppressed Item D remains at 144pt while Item E returns to its own 144pt origin. Bullet suppression removes the dot without changing other labels. Earlier-trigger, root-level and no-patch controls retain their labels. Thirteen current pages pass layout at 0.5pt and searchable content/order/census. The two level-2 restart 8/9 pages still label Item E/G (1)/(1) instead of native (2)/(3), tracked in #2094; their markers and body positions otherwise match. Every page retains one Letter page, a Cambria 14pt bold heading, 11pt regular black body text, expected parenthesis/bracket styles and physical paragraph gaps. No shapes, fills, strokes/borders or hairlines <=1pt, rotation, italic, underline, clipping, overflow or missing body text appear. All fifteen strict raster reports have zero material clusters, which does not waive the two text mismatches. Diff fragments are glyph edges and sub-material baseline/pitch drift (at most 0.201pt/0.136pt), tracked in #1874. No other material finding remains untracked.",
